# Scope-specific .gitignore for graphify. Same syntax as .gitignore.
# Mirrors what `.gitignore` (root + nested) excludes from git, with
# extra graphify-only patterns (lockfiles, large fixtures) on top.
#
# Pattern strategy: wildcard `**/foo/` so any future `Dimmy.X.csproj`
# or `core/Y` subproject gets the same hygiene without an edit here.
# Burned 2026-05-30: a third Win project (Dimmy.Windows.UiTests) added
# 53 nodes of `obj/project.assets.json` to the graph because we'd only
# listed the two known projects explicitly.

# .NET / MSBuild build artefacts — wildcarded so every csproj is covered
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/publish/

# Rust / Cargo build artefacts
**/target/

# Xcode / Swift build artefacts
platforms/macos/build/
platforms/macos/DerivedData/
**/Dimmy.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
**/Dimmy.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
**/*.xcuserstate
**/*.xcuserdatad/

# Linux native build (GTK4) artefacts
platforms/linux/target/

# Mac AppleDouble metadata extracted from zip — `._*` placeholders + __MACOSX/
**/__MACOSX/
**/._*

# Generated by us (core build script) — Rust binding shims, not source
core/gen/

# An exploratory new-Mac mockup that lives untracked.
mockup/

# Graphify outputs (recursive — graphify-out/graph.html, cache, ecc.)
graphify-out/

# Lockfiles — they list dependencies, not source structure
Cargo.lock
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock

# Test audio fixtures (data, not code/docs)
*.wav
*.ogg
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.mov
tests/audio/
tests/test_audio.wav

# Installer / package artefacts (also blocked by root .gitignore)
*.exe
*.msi
*.dmg
*.AppImage
*.deb
*.nupkg
dist/
node_modules/

# Local env / secrets — .gitignore covers these but defence in depth
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.staging
.DS_Store
.cargo/
